    "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo commits, ordered dependency: a **prerequisite hotfix** (User-Agent header) plus the **ADR-021 specification** (real-page interaction).\n\nThese are together because they're causally linked: loading Wikipedia to gather motivation for ADR-021 failed with 403 until the UA fix. Without the fix, the test that revealed both ADR-021 issues (no scrolling, hover freezes) was impossible to run. The UA fix is 13 lines and fully verified; the ADR documents the issues Wikipedia exposed.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Commit | What | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cab3564` | `fix(net): add User-Agent header` | libcurl's default UA (`curl/8.x`) is blocked by Wikipedia per their UA policy → 403 on every real-world fetch. Fix: send a proper identifying UA. |\n| `ef0dffa` | `docs(adr): add ADR-021 real-page interaction` | Specification for the two issues Wikipedia's 800KB page surfaced. |\n\n## ADR-021 — what it specifies\n\nTwo coordinated design decisions, because they touch the same handlers and fixing only one leaves a half-broken browser:\n\n### Change 1: Scrolling via Gtk::ScrolledWindow\n\nWrap `m_drawing_area` in `Gtk::ScrolledWindow`. After every `relayout()`, set the DrawingArea's size request to `(viewport_width, layout_root.height)`. GTK then provides scrollbars, mouse wheel, trackpad, keyboard scrolling for free.\n\n**Critical invariant preserved**: hit-test, hover, and click coordinates remain in layout space — GDK translates automatically via widget hierarchy. ADR-018/019/020's coordinate handling needs **no changes**.\n\n**Fallback documented**: if GTK4 empirically rejects ~60,000px DrawingArea heights for Wikipedia, manual scroll offset engages (translate paint origin, add offset to incoming hit-test coords).\n\n### Change 2: Incremental restyle for hover\n\nCurrent `on_mouse_motion` calls `relayout()` on every hover change — which re-runs the *full* pipeline (extract CSS, cascade, layout, line-break, Pango-measure, rebuild box tree). <1ms on link-test pages, **several hundred ms to seconds on Wikipedia** → UI freezes, hover colors never appear, clicks during freeze are swallowed, URL bar stays focused.\n\nNew `RenderPipeline::restyle(state)`:\n- Re-run **cascade only** (skip layout entirely; ~10ms even on 800KB)\n- Walk existing layout tree updating colors in place from the new cascade output\n- `on_mouse_motion` calls `restyle()` instead of `relayout()`\n\n**Invariant established**: restyle never changes node dimensions. Testable; documented v1 limitation (hover can only affect color — if author CSS sets `a:hover { font-size: larger }`, restyle produces stale layout; deferred to future ADR).\n\n### Backfilled change: LayoutText::element\n\nAdd `const dom::Element* element` to `LayoutText`, populated at creation in `layout.cpp`'s text-only path. Mirrors ADR-018's `LineFragment::element` addition — same design shape, same purpose (link text nodes back to source element for restyle color updates).\n\n## Key design decisions worth reviewing\n\n1. **ScrolledWindow vs manual offset** — committed to ScrolledWindow. Rationale: coordinate translation handled once by GDK vs reimplemented in every handler (bug-prone); free scrollbar rendering; free wheel/keyboard. Manual offset documented as fallback if GTK rejects 60,000px heights.\n2. **Restyle can't change sizes (v1)** — Restyle is cascade-only; if `:hover` ever affects sizes, stale layout. Acceptable because the UA stylesheet's only hover rule changes color. Author CSS via `<style>` could theoretically break this, documented as v1 limitation.\n3. **LayoutText::element backfill** — touches ADR-016 territory (LayoutText struct). Mirrors ADR-018's precedent. Alternative (walking parent chain at restyle time) is fragile. My preference: backfill, and note in the ADR.\n\n## Verification plan (in the follow-up implementation PR)\n\nUnit tests:\n- `LayoutText::element` populated for text-only content\n- Restyle with same state does not change `(x, y, width, height)` — asserts the \"restyle never changes layout dimensions\" invariant\n- Restyle with `hovered_element` set updates fragment colors; others unchanged\n\nVisual (Wikipedia, 800KB page):\n- Scroll from top to bottom (previously inaccessible)\n- Hover link → instant color change (previously froze)\n- Click link → navigates (previously swallowed by freeze)\n- Back → returns (scroll resets to top — documented limitation)\n- `:visited` update: Back shows clicked link as purple\n- Small page (link-test-a) — no regression; no scrollbar (fits viewport)\n\n## Test count\n\n- Current: **253 cases / 986 assertions**, all pass (unchanged — the UA fix has no test impact; the ADR is docs)\n- After implementation lands: +N new restyle tests\n\n## Deferred\n\n- Scroll position restoration on Back/Forward (separate ADR)\n- Hover affects sizes (would break restyle invariant; separate ADR)\n- Horizontal scrolling (v1 is single-column vertical only)\n- Scroll anchoring during resize (v1 scrolls to top)\n- Partial repaint (v1 full-visible-region repaint; acceptable at 10-50ms)\n- Scroll-driven CSS (`:scroll-timeline` etc.)\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/021-real-page-interaction.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n",
